        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Xawery Żuławski, Brian G. Hutton, Dorota Masłowska\n- Films: Polish-Russian War, Where Eagles Dare, Kelly's Heroes\n- Places: Warsaw\n- Roles: film director, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Brian G. Hutton was born on January 1, 1935, and he was an American actor and film director.\n- Xawery Żuławski was born on December 22, 1971, in Warsaw, and he is a Polish film director.\n- Polish-Russian War is a 2009 Polish film directed by Xawery Żuławski.\n- Polish-Russian War was based on the novel Polish-Russian War under the white-red flag by Dorota Masłowska.\n- Brian G. Hutton's most notable directing credits include the action films Where Eagles Dare (1968) and Kelly's Heroes (1970).\n- Brian G. Hutton died on August 19, 2014.",
